 "notes": "ACTION-UFC-05 v4, approved 2026-09-17. Backfilled from the surviving scratch on 2026-09-17 under the RENDER-01 Part 5-8 archiving rule.\n\nSINGLE SUBJECT: load_inst() returns zeros for anything but 'knight', so inputs/matte_knight/ is the only matte set the build reads -- the opponent is world, and the world is what gets dimmed.\n\nNO KIT AT APPROVAL TIME. UFC-05 predates the kit YAML: its constants were inline in w2_build4.py plus inputs/grade_solved.json (world 0.44, subj 1.45, vignette 0.30, solved against the reference's OUTPUT luma for this source). inputs/impact_kit_snapshot.yaml is therefore NOT the kit that rendered this reel -- it is the port's kit as of the archive date, kept so Port 8 can compare the values it will use against the ones that shipped.\n\ninputs/clean/ are the graded, cropped frames the effects read; the 151 MB of pre-crop source frames are NOT archived, being derivable from the source clip plus inputs/plan.json.\n\n2026-09-17: inputs/subject.json backfilled with the FULL HSV subject_colour spec. Recording hue_deg alone let the worker default the sat/val floors, which is the documented failure mode for a dark garment.\n\n2026-09-18: TWO PLANS, and the first backfill archived only one.\n  inputs/plan.json      \u2014 u1/plan.json, what w2_build4.py reads for the push/framing\n                          (mag 1.7778).\n  inputs/crop_plan.json \u2014 w2/plan.json, what w2_crop.py used to cut clean/ and m/\n                          from the native frames (mag 2.0361, cx 0.6552, src_h 943).\nThis is the one crop_rect_for() needs: warping the native mattes through it\nreproduces the archived portrait mattes at IoU 1.0000 on 96/96. The gate table's\n'magnification 2.0361x' is the crop plan's, not plan.json's \u2014 which is how the\nmismatch was caught.\nsrc_h=943 is uniform and equals chrome.json's video_rect height (the chrome band\nstarts at y=943), so it is derivable from the archive even without this file.",
